# Architecture & content

## Stack

Next.js App Router + React + TypeScript + Tailwind + shadcn/ui + Motion → Vercel. TS/TSX only.

Layers: `app/` `components/` `sections/` `ui/` `motion/` `hooks/` `lib/` `data/` `styles/` `public/`

## Server / Client boundaries

**SSR as much content as practical. Hydrate only the interaction that needs it.**

- Server Components by default
- Explicit `"use client"` islands for interaction
- Do **not** use `dynamic(..., { ssr:false })` from arbitrary Server Components as a generic escape
- If `ssr:false` is required, dynamic-import from an appropriate Client Component
- Animation ≠ disable SSR; Motion can live in scoped Client Components under server content shells

## Signature loading

Separate modules: `SignatureStoryShell` · `DesktopLaptopStory` · `MobileLayerStory` · `ReducedMotionStory`

- Client/responsive loading boundary — no fragile server viewport detection
- No hydration mismatch; no UA sniffing unless unavoidable; no duplicate active scenes
- Mobile must not pay desktop laptop runtime/download cost

## Content

- Typed `data/` modules for major copy — do not invent achievements
- Verified claims: 7.8 yrs · 30% load · 14+ GSAT modules · React/TS/RN
- Caprus client “Present” inconsistency: prefer employment dates until confirmed
- Internal `/design-system`: noindex, not in nav/sitemap

## Metadata

Typed `lib/site.ts` from `NEXT_PUBLIC_SITE_URL`. Never invent domains. Never ship prod canonical/OG pointing at localhost.

## Testing

Early: typecheck, lint, prod build, a11y sanity, responsive QA. Later Playwright for nav, ⌘K, anchors, reduced-motion, signature entry/exit, keyboard, case studies. Don’t overbuild tests in scaffolding.
